//! The synthetic support suite: generated pre-supported scenes with known truth, read by the
//! backend's support reader and checked stage by stage without DragonFruit.
//!
//! Every case of `support_synthetic/variants.txt` (122 cases, each with variants by side count,
//! rotation and style) is generated by a port of the prototype's generator (`cases.rs`, `scene.rs`,
//! `geom.rs`; it reproduces the prototype's meshes and truth exactly), read, and checked:
//! - validate: the truth itself (its surface on the mesh, closed welds, truth loops);
//! - stage 1 "reader labels": the reader's elements against the truth parts (axis, width, label);
//! - stage 2 "layout": counts, contacts, sockets, widths, routes and brace ends against the truth;
//! - stage 4 on a nominal build (`nominal.rs`, the layout meshed roughly as DragonFruit builds it):
//!   4a clips (no build triangle inside the model but tips) and 4b contact loops.
//!
//! Stage 3 (recall and precision of DragonFruit's own build) and stage 4 on DragonFruit's build
//! need DragonFruit; `backend/tools/support-reader` runs them. Tolerances are the prototype's.
//!
//! The results are held to `support_synthetic/expected.json` (per variant, which stages pass):
//! a stage that stops passing fails the test, and so does one that starts passing, so the file is
//! kept in step (`SYNTHETIC_UPDATE=1 cargo test -p findamodel --test support_synthetic` rewrites
//! it). `SYNTHETIC_DUMP=<dir>` also writes each variant's meshes, truth, reading, layout, nominal
//! build and results there (for `scripts/synthetic-catalogue.py`, which renders the docs'
//! catalogue).
#![allow(dead_code)]

#[path = "support_synthetic/cases.rs"]
mod cases;
#[path = "support_synthetic/geom.rs"]
mod geom;
#[path = "support_synthetic/measure.rs"]
mod measure;
#[path = "support_synthetic/nominal.rs"]
mod nominal;
#[path = "support_synthetic/reading.rs"]
